RUNBOOK 7.2, 7.3 and 8.6: store moves the temporary name to a new name
of its own before it removes it (36A); a foreign entry stays under that
name, and the error says "store: <dir>/.tmp-<...>, moved to
<dir>/.tmp-<...>, is <what>, not the file written, and stays there:
another process changed the directory meanwhile" or "..., moved to
..., is missing: ..."; "... is <what>, not the file written, and
stays: ..." only when the rename to the new name fails. Window 2 is
closed, the narrower window 2' stays; the raw "unlink ...: is a
directory" after a link is gone; ENOSPC at the rename leaves the own
temporary file for the next publish. RUNBOOK 0.2: a real directory
_*, .* or testdata goes to skippedTagged without os.Stat, with the
churn figures (36B).

DECISIONS: addendum 36 A to D93 (dropTemp, window 2', a failing rename
or unlink, tests, races, the study of item 128 with the hold point on
store.WriteAccept); in addendum 34 A the head names 124 as the same
class as 108 when writing, and WritePrivateFileAtomicIn is no longer
called a path variant. AUDIT: addendum 36g, R17 (b) after task 36, R35
after task 36 with H1 of the review of 36B, two rows in 6.2. HANDOFF:
addendum 36g, known limits of publish with window 2' and item 128,
point 1 with the third state, points 7 and 9 (new hold point
WriteAccept without the mailbox lock). Backlog after M1: addendum 36g;
125 and 127 partly done, 128 with the result of the study, new 129
(H1 and H2 of the review of 36B). Hints F1 to F5 of the review of 34g.

